ho are the Zapotecs in Mexico? The Valley Zapotecs, who occupy the fertile Valley of Oaxaca in the center of the state. The Sierra Zapotecs (Mountain Zapotecs), who occupy the districts of Ixtlán, Villa Alta, and Choapán in the Sierra Norte. The Isthmus Zapotecs, who live on the tropical Isthmus of Tehuantepec, which is the narrowest part of the Mexican Republic. How many Zapotec people live in Oaxaca? If you count the various subsidiary Mixtec languages, the total Mixtec-speaking population of the Mexican Republic in 2000 included 444,498 individuals. The Zapotec ethnic group remains the largest indigenous group of Oaxaca and presently occupies 67 municipios of Oaxaca.","Zapotec, Mixtepec",Otomanguean
